  "scope": "Complete affine/projective subsection at the recorded mixed fresh/reused first-read scope: original five inputs retained from complete 424 reads, new 115-line input and changed 73-line probability input freshly read; all six final inputs freshly reread after 26 actual final images. Chapter 33 seam lines 79--87. No fresh whole recursive Chapter12/33 certification.",
  "mathematical_boundary": "At fixed affine points and positive growth, continuous weights have compact active-pair stability and joint one-sided derivatives stable under convergent uniform/scalar directions. Left/right growth slopes are maximum/minimum active constants; growth kinks are countable for each fixed point and weight. Weight Gateaux differentiability is exactly unique active probability. A disk quadratic weight has an explicit corner. No zero-growth, common-all-points countability, Frechet, absolute-continuity, novelty or original-problem-closure claim.",
